        "problem": "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7{x}^{2}+20x+3}{(3x+2)(x-1)(x+5)}=\\frac{A}{(3x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)}+\\frac{C}{(x+5)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are real constants, calculate $A+B+C.$",
        "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7{x}^{2}+20x+3}{(3x+2)(x-1)(x+5)}=\\frac{A}{(3x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)}+\\frac{C}{(x+5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(3x+2)(x-1)(x+5)$ gives\n\n$$\n7{x}^{2}+20x+3=A(x-1)(x+5)+B(3x+2)(x+5)+C(3x+2)(x-1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{2}{3}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{(-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}+20(-\\frac{2}{3})+3 & =A(-\\frac{2}{3}-1)(-\\frac{2}{3}+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(3(-\\frac{2}{3})+2)(-\\frac{2}{3}+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(3(-\\frac{2}{3})+2)(-\\frac{2}{3}-1) \\\\ \\frac{28}{9}-\\frac{40}{3}+3 & =A(-\\frac{65}{9}) \\\\ -\\frac{65}{9} & =A(-\\frac{65}{9}) \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(1)^{2}+20(1)+3 & =A(1-1)(1+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(3(1)+2)(1+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(3(1)+2)(1-1) \\\\ 7+20+3 & =B(30) \\\\ B & =\\frac{30}{30} \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(-5)^{2}+20(-5)+3 & =A(-5-1)(-5+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(3(-5)+2)(-5+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(3(-5)+2)(-5-1) \\\\ 175-100+3 & =C(78) \\\\ C & =\\frac{78}{78} \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B+C=1+1+1=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
